    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. for the live load, i'm mostly worried about the snow load and people crowding the edge. if i have a potential weak point in the beam span or if the joists look like they might sag over time, what are the main structural red flags i should be looking out for in my calculations?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A major red flag is when the calculated deflection under the maximum specified live load exceeds the allowable deflection limits, which often relate to the span and material type. You should also check the shear stress in the beams to ensure it doesn't exceed the beam's capacity, especially near supports. If the beam size is inadequate for the tributary area it supports, you are likely undersizing it for both bending and deflection. Always confirm your design adheres to the governing span tables for your lumber grade and beam spacing.",
      "source": "target",
