      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it, thanks. one more thing—is there any way to account for unexpected fatigue or sudden, weird structural failures that aren't part of the standard math? like, as a builder, how do i prepare for those things that just seem to happen out of nowhere even when the load math looks perfect?",
